From: postmarketOS <bramble@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: do not switch to the suspend console on suspend

The kernel switches to a suspend console (tty63) before it suspends, and
back to the old console after resume, unless every framebuffer says that
it does not need this (fb_info->skip_vt_switch). The msm framebuffer did
not say so. With a Wayland session this switch is a problem: elogind
pauses the DRM device and resumes it again, wlroots destroys the output on
the pause and adds a new one on the resume, and Phosh builds its whole UI
again for the new output. On the Pixel 4a (5G) this takes more than the
3 s that phoc waits for the layer surfaces to answer. phoc then removes
Phosh from the compositor (a late answer hits its assertion in
phoc_layout_transaction_notify_layer_configured), Phosh exits with code 1,
gnome-session ends the session, and the user is logged out at every
resume. The new output also switches the screen on after the resume.

Android has no VT. The display driver does not need the console switch:
sde_kms_pm_suspend() keeps a copy of the display state and
sde_kms_pm_resume() commits it again.

---
--- a/techpack/display/msm/msm_fbdev.c
+++ b/techpack/display/msm/msm_fbdev.c
@@ -132,6 +132,14 @@
 
 	strlcpy(fbi->fix.id, "msm", sizeof(fbi->fix.id));
 
+	/*
+	 * Do not let suspend switch to the suspend console and back. The switch
+	 * makes elogind pause and resume the DRM device, wlroots destroys and
+	 * re-adds the output, and Phosh builds its whole UI again while phoc
+	 * waits for it. phoc drops Phosh after 3 s. Android has no VT either.
+	 */
+	fbi->skip_vt_switch = true;
+
 	drm_fb_helper_fill_fix(fbi, fb->pitches[0], fb->format->depth);
 	drm_fb_helper_fill_var(fbi, helper, sizes->fb_width, sizes->fb_height);
 
